# Layrus Labs — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development (git-ignored), and set the same names in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for production. Nothing here is
# needed to build or serve the site; only the assistant reads them.

# ── The assistant ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a key the chat route answers 503 with a message rather than failing
# in a way nobody can read.

# Option A — Anthropic directly. Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Option B — DeepSeek, which serves an Anthropic-compatible endpoint, so the
# same code runs against it with no changes. The model name below still says
# claude-opus-5-5: DeepSeek maps claude-opus* to deepseek-v4-pro and
# claude-sonnet*/claude-haiku* to deepseek-flash, so leave it alone.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<your deepseek key>

# Which model to ask for. Defaults to claude-opus-5-5, which both providers
# understand. Pin a specific one here only if you want something else.
# LYRA_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# ── Spend control ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set a monthly limit on the provider's own dashboard — that is the only real
# ceiling on this endpoint. The route's rate limit is per-instance and
# best-effort; see the note in app/api/chat/route.ts.
